course: dictionary
lesson: 8005
title: Reduction: less, lower and simpler
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reduction comes from the verb reduce, which means to make something smaller or less. A reduction can be the act of making something smaller, or the amount it has gone down by. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: In a shop, a reduction is a lower price, also called a discount. «The shop gave a big reduction on all coats this week» means the coats cost less. In maths, a reduction can mean a smaller picture, or a fraction made simpler. The sentence around the word tells you which one it is.
explain: Sometimes the words around a reduction hide what really happened. «A company that sacks two hundred people may announce a headcount reduction, as if it only changed a number on a chart.» The clues are sacks and two hundred people. Headcount reduction sounds neat, but it means people lost their jobs.
fact: Reduction means making something smaller, less or lower.
fact: «Reduction» can mean a lower price in a shop, which is another word for discount.
fact: In maths, a fraction can be simplified by reduction: 6/8 reduces to 3/4.
fact: «Headcount reduction» is a company's way of saying that fewer people work there.
fact: Reduce, reuse and recycle are ways to cut down waste, which is a reduction in rubbish.
exercise: «The shop had a big reduction on all shoes this week.» What does reduction mean here? | A new shoe design | A bigger shop | A long queue | *A lower price
exercise: In maths, simplifying 6/8 is a reduction. What is 6/8 reduced to? | 8/6 | 1/8 | 6/4 | *3/4
exercise: A reduction in noise means the noise is | The same | Longer | *Quieter | Louder
test: A company that sacks two hundred people may announce «a headcount reduction». What is the plain meaning? | The company hired more people | The company moved to a new town | *Two hundred people lost their jobs | The chart was changed
test: «The car made a reduction in speed.» What does this mean? | *The car slowed down | The car drove faster | The car changed colour | The car stopped for lunch
exam: A shop makes a £10 reduction on a £40 coat. What is the new price? | £40 | *£30 | £10 | £50
